== H1: algebra of F and of the extremal condition ==
  [OK] F(-x) = -G(x) - h^2 identically (so F(-x) <= -h^2 < 0 on the whole conformal boundary y = -x)
  [OK] F(1/(3 s)) = 0 (double root, F' = 0 there)  <=>  h^2 = -1 + 1/(27*s**2)  <=>  27 s^2 (1 + h^2) = 1
  [OK] this is the Dias-Lemos extremal condition 27 m^2 A^2 = 1 - 9 m^2 Lambda (hep-th/0301046, section III B), reproduced independently
  [OK] CONTROL (wrong claim must be rejected): control: 27 s^2 (1 + h^2) = 1 is NOT 27 s^2 = 1 (that would be the Lambda = 0 saturation)
  [OK] with F_max saturation 27 s^2 = 1 the extremal condition gives h^2 = 0: a static region needs Lambda = 0

== H2: real-root structure on a grid of the allowed region 27 s^2 (1 + h^2) < 1 ==
  [OK] 2301 grid points: three real roots y1 < -x_n < ... < -x_s < y2 < 1/(3s) < y3 everywhere: exactly TWO horizons (y2, y3) inside the physical range y >= -x; the third root is outside it (max of y1 + x_n = -8.2493e-6 < 0, min of y2 + x_s = 6.2456e-5 > 0)
  [OK] so in the dS C-metric with Lambda > 0 there is NO separate acceleration horizon: y2 is the acceleration horizon and the cosmological horizon at once (as Dias-Lemos state); the brief's T_acc = T_cosm is therefore not a condition
  [OK] Descartes: coefficients of r f(r) have signs [-1, 1, 1, -1]: 2 sign changes => at most 2 positive roots (Lambda > 0, m > 0)
  [OK] CONTROL (wrong claim must be rejected): control: for the AdS sign of Lambda (coefficient signs [1, 1, 1, -1]) the count is different (1 sign change), i.e. the dS conclusion is not a generic-cubic accident

== H3: thermal equilibrium T_bh = T_(acc/cosm)  (C5) ==
  [OK] F'(y2)/F'(y3) = (-y1 + y2)/(y1 - y3): |T_(acc/cosm)/T_bh| = (y2 - y1)/(y3 - y1)
  [OK] T_(acc/cosm)/T_bh < 1 strictly on all 2301 non-degenerate grid points (both temperatures for the SAME Killing vector d_t): the black-hole horizon is always hotter; equality only at y2 = y3 (degenerate/extremal), where both vanish
  [OK] approaching the extremal boundary the ratio tends to 1: 1.0
  [OK] m = 0: T(y2) = sqrt(h**2 + 1)/(2*pi) (units of A) = sqrt(A^2 + H^2)/(2 pi): the Unruh-de Sitter effective temperature of an accelerated observer
  [OK] outcome of C5: T_bh = T_(acc/cosm) has no non-degenerate solution: label = same set as C4 (ENDPOINT/boundary), never an interior point

